{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Technique Aggregation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Technique Aggregation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"forensic technique aggregation forensic technique aggregation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Technique Aggregation.md","fileName":"Forensic Technique Aggregation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Forensic Technique Aggregation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Image Authenticity and Forensic Reasoning","Image Authenticity","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Technique Aggregation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Technique Aggregation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"forensic technique aggregation forensic technique aggregation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Forensic Technique Aggregation.md","fileName":"Forensic Technique Aggregation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Forensic Technique Aggregation","heading":"Forensic Technique Aggregation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Forensic technique aggregation combines multiple analyses whose evidence arises from different parts of the imaging pipeline. Metadata inspection, lighting geometry, compression history, resampling detection, and camera-sensor analysis can each test a different necessary condition of the proposed photograph.\n\nAgreement among independent tests increases confidence because a forger must preserve many subtle regularities at once. Aggregation still does not prove [[Image Authenticity]]: correlated tests may share assumptions, benign processing may disturb several traces, and an informed forger may deliberately conceal them.","tags":["baby"],"link